00:05:24.561 --> 00:05:26.310
PARESH KHARYA: Thanks
a lot for having me.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.560
MELANIE WARRICK: So tell us
a little about who you are

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.050
and what you do over at NVIDIA.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:30.883
PARESH KHARYA: Sure.

00:05:30.883 --> 00:05:33.800
So I'm Paresh Kharya,
responsible for product

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.454
marketing for our
data center products.

00:05:36.454 --> 00:05:37.370
MELANIE WARRICK: Nice.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.420
MARK MANDEL: Fantastic.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.990
And I know you're here
today, NVIDIA's here today.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.257
There's a big NVIDIA presence.

00:05:42.257 --> 00:05:44.090
Can you tell us about
what that's all about?

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:45.173
PARESH KHARYA: Yeah, sure.

00:05:45.173 --> 00:05:49.880
So my company, NVIDIA, invented
the GPU two decades ago

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:53.716
that basically revolutionized
the modern computer graphics.

00:05:53.716 --> 00:05:54.590
MELANIE WARRICK: Yes.

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:56.840
PARESH KHARYA: And also
revolutionized parallel

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:57.890
computing.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:01.910
More recently, deep
learning powered by the GPUs

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.860
have been responsible
for advancements

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:05.580
in artificial intelligence.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.460
And we are very
happy about that.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:10.730
GPU computing is also
available across all

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:13.820
the different computing
form factors from desktops

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:18.050
to devices to servers to cloud
services from our partners

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:18.810
like Google.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.310
MELANIE WARRICK:
You're here at Next

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:22.324
because you had a big
announcement yesterday.

00:06:22.324 --> 00:06:23.990
Can you tell us a
little bit about that?

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:24.440
PARESH KHARYA: Yeah, sure.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.010
We're very excited about that.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.890
So we announced that our
Tesla P4 GPUs are coming

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.870
to Google Cloud Platform.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:36.950
P4 is basically a small form
factor, highly specialized

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:40.040
for AI inference workloads GPU.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.720
And while our GPUs--

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:43.490
flagship GPUs like V100--

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:45.890
have been available
for a while, Google

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:48.590
is the first cloud
platform to make

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.390
P4 available on a global scale.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.180
And this speaks to
the tipping point

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:58.820
of how AI inference is becoming
really important as a workload.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:02.930
Now, P4 is ideally suited
for the real time inference

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.060
workloads that require
really fast processing.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:09.470
So think of services like
speech-based interfaces,

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.130
or real time live translations,
understanding of video,

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.090
and so on.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:17.000
P4 can process AI
workloads that are really

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.582
complex 40 times faster than
what's possible on CPUs alone.

00:07:21.582 --> 00:07:22.790
MELANIE WARRICK: That's fast.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.320
Well, you probably
heard us talk about this

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.390
in the past in regards to
inference and training.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:29.480
But Paresh, do you mind
explaining just briefly

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.560
what is inference?

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:30.740
PARESH KHARYA: Yeah.

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:31.800
That's a great question.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.900
So training a neural network
is when you're basically

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:40.100
pumping in a lot of data to
help a neural network learn

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.680
by taking a look at the
data and the labels that

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.880
are associated with data.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.130
So that's the training step.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.600
It's computationally
very complex.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.450
Inference is when you're putting
that trained neural network

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:51.410
to work.

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:54.810
So it looks at new data,
and it makes predictions.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:58.040
So for example, if it's
about recognizing speech,

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.680
it's taking in a
new spoken sentence.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.280
And it's able to recognize it.

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:03.565
So that's the AI inference.

00:08:03.565 --> 00:08:04.940
MARK MANDEL: That's
really great.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:08.450
We should also note that
we have episode 119 where

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.314
we talk to Bryan Catanzaro
from NVIDIA, talking

00:08:11.314 --> 00:08:12.480
about deep learning as well.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.240
So people want to hear more
about that kind of thing

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:14.720
as well.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:15.890
MELANIE WARRICK:
Agreed, definitely.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.260
Well, what do you enjoy--
what have you enjoyed or seen

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.810
so far that you've been
excited about outside

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:21.967
of the announcement?

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:23.300
PARESH KHARYA: Yeah, absolutely.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.980
So one of the really
exciting things

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.590
for me personally is
Google's pioneering use

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:31.580
of artificial intelligence in
adding magic to your services,

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:32.120
like--

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:32.840
MELANIE WARRICK: Oh, magic.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.798
PARESH KHARYA: Exactly.

00:08:33.798 --> 00:08:36.230
Whether it's the G
Suite or optimizing

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:39.710
the performance of your data
centers-- massive data centers.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:42.260
And Google is not just keeping
its technology to itself.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:45.260
It's basically making it
available to everyone,

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:49.290
every industry, and enabling
them to be transformed by AI.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:52.580
Google and NVIDIA, we
have a strong partnership.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.120
And we both understand the
need for accelerated computing

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.710
to help advance AI.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:01.410
And Google continues to
invest in DPUs, for example.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:04.490
But at the same time, Google
is also relying on GPUs

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:07.250
to power its own internal
AI, as well as they are

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.530
making it available as a cloud
service on the Google Cloud

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:11.390
Platform.

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:15.440
So every deep learning framework
and the diversity of modern AI

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.100
can be supported.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.350
MELANIE WARRICK: That's great.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.930
Well, we appreciate you
coming by to chat with us

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:21.680
on the podcast.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.197
Anything else you wanted to
mention before we let you go?

00:09:24.197 --> 00:09:25.030
PARESH KHARYA: Yeah.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.210
It's a really exciting time.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.030
We are witnessing
a new revolution

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:30.860
in terms of artificial
intelligence

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:34.550
and what it can do to
revolutionize the workflows

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.450
and simplify our lives, as well
as revolutionize industries.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.700
And we're just at
the tipping point

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.370
right now where
people are realizing

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.940
all of this is possible.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.150
We're very happy
to work with Google

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:49.700
to make our GPU
computing technology

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:52.070
available through the
Google Cloud Platform

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.582
to help companies and
industries transform themselves.

00:09:55.582 --> 00:09:56.540
MARK MANDEL: Fantastic.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.820
Well, thank you so much
for coming to join us here

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.020
